From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: scuggo <scuggo@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 29 May 2026 21:59:52 +0400
Subject: [PATCH] EXPERIMENTAL: drm/msm: eDP variable refresh (AVR) behind msm.vrr_enabled

Expose "vrr_capable" on the eDP connector and program the DPU INTF
Adaptive Refresh (AVR) block so the panel can run its EDID monitor range
(24-120 Hz on the Sharp LQ138P1JX61) instead of a fixed rate:

 - dpu_9_2_x1e80100.h: DPU_INTF_AVR feature bit on the DP/eDP INTFs
 - dpu_hw_intf.c/.h: setup_avr (INTF_AVR_VTOTAL from the monitor minimum
   frequency), avr_ctrl (INTF_AVR_CONTROL/MODE), avr_trigger
 - dpu_encoder*.c: carry vrr_enabled/vrr_min_fps to the video encoder,
   program AVR at timing setup and trigger it at enable
 - dpu_crtc.c: VRR_ENABLED changes force a modeset
 - dp_ctrl.c: set MSA_TIMING_PAR_IGNORE_EN in DOWNSPREAD_CTRL when the
   sink advertises MSA_TIMING_PAR_IGNORED (DPCD 0x007 bit 6)
 - dp_drm.c/dp_panel.c: attach and set "vrr_capable" from the EDID range

Adapted from scuggo's msm-vrr-avr.patch for Linux 7.2.8: all hunks apply,
the dp_drm.c hunk was rebased, and everything is gated behind a new module
parameter, msm.vrr_enabled (default 0, read-only at runtime). With the
default the kernel behaves as before: no vrr_capable property, no MSA
ignore, no AVR programming. The patch is untested by upstream on this
panel; expect rough edges (see the omarchy-sl7-test-entry VRR preset).

Origin: https://github.com/scuggo/x1e-nixos kernel/modules/msm-vrr/msm-vrr-avr.patch (HEAD ca7db70, 2026-07-01); scuggo (GPL-2.0 kernel patch)
Upstream-Status: Inappropriate (experimental; mainline msm has no vrr_capable for these DPUs, the msm.vrr_enabled gate is local)

---
diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/disp/dpu1/catalog/dpu_9_2_x1e80100.h b/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/disp/dpu1/catalog/dpu_9_2_x1e80100.h
